1
00:00:07,990 --> 00:01:07,790
You're Tops

2
00:01:07,790 --> 00:01:10,470
Is that you, Susan?

3
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:12,660
It's me, Grandpa.

4
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,430
Am I glad to see you!

5
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:17,730
And am I glad to see you!

6
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:21,280
I am also glad to be here.

7
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,280
How are things?

8
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:26,190
I have been talking to a group of salesmen

9
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:27,750
since ten this morning,

10
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:30,950
and I'm real exhausted.

11
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:33,470
Well, you look good.

12
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:34,660
What's Harry doing tonight?

13
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:35,130
He and Michelle

14
00:01:35,130 --> 00:01:38,120
are visiting relatives in New Jersey today.

15
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:40,640
The rest of our family went to the movies.

16
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:43,920
So it's just you and me, Susan.

17
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,810
It's nice to be alone with you, Grandpa.

18
00:01:46,810 --> 00:01:48,650
We don't get to see enough of each other.

19
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,800
Oh, I feel the same way, Susan.

20
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,530
I miss seeing you.

21
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,330
But to tell the truth,

22
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:56,580
next time

23
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:58,590
I'd like to go into the city and meet you there,

24
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:01,900
instead of you coming here.

25
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:03,580
You don't need to do that, Grandpa.

26
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:05,620
Yeah, I do.

27
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:09,680
I need to get out more.

28
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:11,860
Well, I mean

29
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,930
there's a lot to do around the house,

30
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:15,630
and I love being here with the family,

31
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:16,360
you know,

32
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:20,780
but I'm restless.

33
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,790
Since I retired,

34
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:25,750
I've got extra time on my hands.

35
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:29,040
I understand, Grandpa.

36
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:31,190
I think you do.

37
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:32,880
Frankly,

38
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:36,210
I'd like to use my brain a little more.

39
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:37,470
Grandpa,

40
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:42,030
you have so much energy and so many years of experience.

41
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:45,160
There are probably a lot of places for you to work

42
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,180
Particularly in the construction field.

43
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,220
But at my age,

44
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:52,850
I'm not looking for a full-time job.

45
00:02:52,850 --> 00:02:55,980
I'm retired.

46
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:57,320
But I'm bored.

47
00:02:57,320 --> 00:03:02,960
Well, there must be something.

48
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:07,270
Maybe I can help.

49
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:09,240
Let's go into the kitchen,

50
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:12,670
and maybe you can help me set the table.

51
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:14,110
Sounds good to me.

52
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:15,240
What are we having?

53
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:17,440
I prepared lamb chops,

54
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:20,700
mashed potatoes, and a tossed green salad to begin with.

55
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:34,040
Grandpa, you are a terrific guy!

56
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,710
You're still thinking about something to do, aren't you?

57
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:38,110
A job of some kind.

58
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:40,060
That's right.

59
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:44,270
I've been thinking about it for weeks now.

60
00:03:44,270 --> 00:03:49,260
There must be some way to put my mind to good use.

61
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,790
We'll find a solution.

62
00:03:50,790 --> 00:03:52,290
A positive solution

63
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:55,290
to your finding a way to use that wonderful mind of yours.
